Fixed. In `src/PhpSpreadsheet/Style/NumberFormat/BaseFormatter.php:15`, `adjustSeparators()` was hard-coding a swap between `.` and `,` whenever the configured separators differed from the defaults. I restored it to use the user-configured separators:

```php
if ($thousandsSeparator !== ',' || $decimalSeparator !== '.') {
    $value = str_replace(['.', ',', "\u{fffd}"], ["\u{fffd}", $thousandsSeparator, $decimalSeparator], $value);
}
```

Validation: `testIssue3900` (the FAIL_TO_PASS case) now passes; Style (882), NumberFormat (116), Calculation (15509), and the directly affected Writer/Shared suites show no regressions — the only remaining errors are pre-existing environment issues (missing `imagejpeg`/GD) confirmed identical on the untouched baseline.
